pervising professor.","linkedByLetter":false,"sections":[{"crn":"54582","code":"","typeCode":"IND","group":"ind","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Independent Study","typeCode":"IND","days":[],"start":null,"end":null,"location":"Location Pending","instructors":[]}],"restrictions":[],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":null,"sectionText":null}]},{"id":"LLS 496","subject":"LLS","number":"496","title":"Seminar in Latina/o Studies","creditHours":"3 OR 4 hours","minHours":3,"genEd":[],"degreeAttributes":"","scheduleNote":"","info":"3 undergraduate hours. 4 graduate hours. May be repeated up to a maximum of 6 undergraduate hours or 12 graduate hours.","linkedByLetter":false,"sections":[{"crn":"57196","code":"AG","typeCode":"LCD","group":"lecture","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Lecture-Discussion","typeCode":"LCD","days":["T"],"start":900,"end":1040,"location":"133 1207 W Oregon","instructors":["Garcia, A"]}],"restrictions":["Restricted to Undergrad - Urbana-Champaign."],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":null,"sectionText":"Topic: Excavations: Latinx Nonfiction and Workshop - Despite the disparate number of Latinx writers being published in the United States, historically and contemporarily, the premise of this class creative nonfiction workshop hinges on the idea that you are the expert of your experience, meaning you are best positioned to tell your life story, and that those stories inherently have worth. As such, we will excavate the most meaningful moments of our lives, the relevant histories that have shaped our personal and communal experiences, and collapse time—the past and the present—to create the most meaningful narratives of our futures. In this class we will investigate the relationships between process and craft, memory and research, fact and truth to explore the personal and public experiences of our diverse lives from the complex communities we inhabit. In addition to reading and discussing published works by contemporary Latinx writers, we will write work and receive feedback from our fellow classmates in workshop. Meets with CW 463"}]},{"id":"LLS 561","subject":"LLS","number":"561","title":"Race and Cultural Critique","creditHours":"4 hours","minHours":4,"genEd":[],"degreeAttributes":"","scheduleNote":"","info":"Same as AAS 561, AFRO 531, ANTH 565, and GWS 561. See AAS 561.","linkedByLetter":false,"sections":[{"crn":"52843","code":"A","typeCode":"LCD","group":"lecture","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Lecture-Discussion","typeCode":"LCD","days":["T"],"start":840,"end":1040,"location":"ARR 1208 W Nevada","instructors":["Rana, J"]}],"restrictions":["Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign."],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":null,"sectionText":"AAS Conference Room Room 1020 1208 W Nevada St, Urbana, IL"}]},{"id":"LLS 590","subject":"LLS","number":"590","title":"Independent Study","creditHours":"1 TO 4 hours","minHours":1,"genEd":[],"degreeAttributes":"","scheduleNote":"","info":"Approved for letter and S/U grading. May be repeated to a maximum of 8 hours.","linkedByLetter":false,"sections":[{"crn":"46522","code":"","typeCode":"IND","group":"ind","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Independent Study","typeCode":"IND","days":[],"start":null,"end":null,"location":"Location Pending","instructors":[]}],"restrictions":["Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign."],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":null,"sectionText":null}]}]